<?php
/**
 * Hub Market — the `FORM_KEY` global, for the RMA pages.
 *
 * CL036-TC36: "When selecting an order to create an RMA request, the products
 * list does not appear ... preventing form submission due to the error
 * 'You must select item RMA'."
 *
 * WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS
 * ---------------------
 * Choosing an order runs `requestOption.findOrder()` (inline in Vnecoms'
 * new_request/js.phtml), which posts to vrma/customer/ajaxproduct through
 * Prototype's `new Ajax.Request(...)`. Reproduced on a seeded complete order,
 * the select fires and then:
 *
 *   ReferenceError: FORM_KEY is not defined
 *     at initialize (legacy-build.min.js)        <- Prototype Ajax.Request
 *     at findOrder  (/en/vrma/customer/new/)
 *
 * and NO request is sent at all. Magento's bundled Prototype reads a global
 * `FORM_KEY` when it builds a POST body. That global is declared only in the
 * admin and vendor areas — Vnecoms' own vendors panel ships it in
 * module-vendors/view/vendors/templates/page/js/require_js.phtml — and nothing
 * declares it on the storefront.
 *
 * So `findOrder()` throws before the request leaves the browser. The list stays
 * empty, and because the select is disabled on the way in and only re-enabled
 * in the AJAX `onSuccess`, it is also left permanently disabled — measured
 * after selecting: `{disabled: true, listHtmlLen: 5}`. With no items rendered
 * there is nothing to tick, which is where "You must select item RMA" comes
 * from on submit. The server side is fine; the request never reaches it.
 *
 * WHY THE VALUE IS READ FROM THE DOM AND NOT FROM PHP
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * The obvious version of this hands the block `Magento\Framework\Data\Form\
 * FormKey` as a layout argument. Magento rejects that — an `xsi:type="object"`
 * argument must implement `View\Element\Block\ArgumentInterface`, and it does
 * not, which fails silently in production with only a log line:
 *
 *   CRITICAL: Instance of ...Block\ArgumentInterface is expected,
 *             got Magento\Framework\Data\Form\FormKey instead.
 *
 * `View\Element\FormKey` cannot be reused either: it hardcodes `_toHtml()` to
 * emit a hidden input and takes no template. Writing a ViewModel of our own
 * would mean a new class, and production runs compiled DI, so it would not be
 * picked up without a di:compile.
 *
 * The page already renders `<input name="form_key">` (verified on the live
 * page), so the key is there to be read. The cookie is the same fallback
 * Magento's own file-uploader.js uses. Deferred to DOMContentLoaded because
 * this block renders before the form; the customer cannot select an order
 * until long after that, so the value is always in place before Prototype
 * asks for it.
 *
 * @var $block \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template
 */
?>
<script>
    (function () {
        'use strict';

        function readFormKey() {
            var input = document.querySelector('input[name="form_key"]'),
                match;

            if (input && input.value) {
                return input.value;
            }

            match = document.cookie.match(/(?:^|;\s*)form_key=([^;]+)/);

            return match ? decodeURIComponent(match[1]) : '';
        }

        function apply() {
            if (!window.FORM_KEY) {
                window.FORM_KEY = readFormKey();
            }
        }

        apply();

        if (!window.FORM_KEY) {
            document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', apply);
        }
    }());
</script>
